  m_Name: Note_Audio_ResonanceEmitter1
  m_EditorClassIdentifier: Assembly-CSharp::NoteData
  title: Resonance Emitter Information
  key: 18
  topic: 1
  boardContentText: 'Resonance emitter is located inside the tidal cave


    Resonance
    emitter transmits low-frequency vibrations into the ocean floor'
  boardSprite: {fileID: 0}
  contentText: 'EMIL: My audio diary. Next entry.

    [pause, breath]

    EMIL:
    I broke the contract. I did it.

    [brief silence]

    EMIL: I signed it.
    Black on white. That I wouldn''t explore the island. That I''d guard it and not
    touch a thing. That it was a national secret.

    [pause]

    EMIL: And look.
    I''ve started uncovering hidden places. Touching things I wasn''t even supposed
    to look at. Experimenting. I even changed the rotation speed of the lighthouse.
    No permission. Just to see what it would do.

    [hesitation]

    EMIL: I''m
    afraid.

    [pause]

    EMIL: But at the same time... I feel alive. Like there''s
    still something in life waiting for me.

    [brief silence]

    EMIL: You know
    that feeling? When you know there''s nothing left waiting for you. A walking
    corpse. Just preparing for death. I had that feeling for years. ...And now suddenly
    it''s gone.

    [longer silence, dripping water]

    EMIL: I found the cave
    by accident. Tidal. The water pulls back in a slow rhythm. Almost as if the cave
    were breathing.

    [pause]

    EMIL: And inside, something is standing. A
    big metal thing, fixed to the floor. It vibrates. You can feel it humming. Everything
    around it shakes, trembles.

    [pause]

    EMIL: That thing sends vibrations
    down. Deep. Into the very floor of the ocean.

    [brief silence]

    EMIL:
    ...Something like an emitter. That''s what I''ll call it. I couldn''t think of
    a better name.

    [pause]

    EMIL: For years I didn''t know about this. And
    it was here the whole time.

    [click]'
  paperSprite: {fileID: 0}
